<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Free State of the Isthmus</h1><p class="st-meta">1840 CE – 1841 CE · capital Panama City</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Panama's first attempt at independence, a breakaway state from New Granada that lasted about a year during the War of the Supremes.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Civil war, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-supremes">War of the Supremes</a>, broke out in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-new-granada">Republic of New Granada</a> in 1839. In November 1840 a popular assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-city">Panama City</a>, cut off from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a>, declared the provinces of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-panama">Panama</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veraguas-province">Veraguas</a> independent as the State of the Isthmus, choosing Colonel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-herrera">Tomás Herrera</a> as head of state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-herrera">Herrera</a>'s government adopted a constitution in 1841, maintained order and sought to protect the isthmus's transit trade between the Atlantic and Pacific, on which its merchants depended. It considered recognition from foreign powers and the possibility of a federal link with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-new-granada">New Granada</a> on its own terms.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When the civil war ended, the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-new-granada">New Granada</a> negotiated Panama's return with promises of greater autonomy. The isthmus was reincorporated on 31 December 1841. The episode was a precedent for Panama's independence in 1903, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-herrera">Herrera</a> is honoured as a national figure.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1840 CE – 1841 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">